One column split in two: the ledger adds both, fills them from the old one,
and drops it. schema.sql then makes them NOT NULL.

== before
CREATE TABLE cook (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO cook VALUES (1, 'Ada Lovelace'), (2, 'Grace Hopper');

== after
CREATE TABLE cook (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, first_name TEXT NOT NULL, last_name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE cook ADD COLUMN first_name TEXT;
ALTER TABLE cook ADD COLUMN last_name TEXT;
UPDATE cook SET
  first_name = substr(name, 1, instr(name, ' ') - 1),
  last_name = substr(name, instr(name, ' ') + 1);
ALTER TABLE cook DROP COLUMN name;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's steps 1 to 4
  step 1
    ALTER TABLE cook ADD COLUMN first_name TEXT;
  step 2
    ALTER TABLE cook ADD COLUMN last_name TEXT;
